corpus/passages/
# At any depth, not just the root: archiving a run moves its corpus under
# archive/, and the root-anchored rule above stopped covering the source text.
**/corpus/passages/
**/corpus/references/
# Working directories of the run in progress. runs/ and judgments/ hold
# translation text and are never committed. pairwise/ and results/ are
# published only when a run closes, by copying them into archive/<run>/ (see
# docs/runbook.md); ignoring the live copies keeps a mid-run `git add -A` from
# committing partial verdicts or a partial leaderboard. Anchored to the root:
# the same names under archive/ are the published copies.
runs/
judgments/
/pairwise/
/results/
manual/
.env
__pycache__/
.venv/
ati.egg-info/
*.egg-info/

# Operator's local corpus working material. Never committed: this project
# publishes rankings, not source text. Anything here is raw novel content or
# scraped metadata staged for `ati add`.
Novel Sources/
raw/
novel_titles.json
wiki_data.json
# Git worktrees created by Claude Code agents live here; never part of the repo.
.claude/worktrees/
